    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOKSJyfM8AAAABQZbo3A",
      "title": "ci: build images with the unified build-images workflow",
      "author": "falcorocks",
      "number": 1029,
      "body": "## Summary\n\n- Replaces the image build caller with the shared `build-images.yaml` reusable workflow from [ethereum-optimism/factory](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/factory), pinned at `9fc2e6aed64fc4acc35dcf967f3746df12cf5e59`. The caller runs on pushes to `main`, release tags (`*/v*`, `v*`), pull requests, merge groups, a daily schedule, and manual dispatch.\n- Converts `.github/images.json` to the version 2 catalog. The same three images are declared with the same registry, Dockerfile, targets, build args, and paths. Adds `default_branch_tags: [\"latest\"]` and `release.publish_tag: \"${version}\"`.\n- Image names and tags are unchanged. A push to `main` publishes `<sha>` and `latest`, as before, plus the branch-name tag `main`. A release tag `<image>/v<semver>` publishes `<sha>` and `v<semver>` with the same `VERSION` build argument as before.\n- Verified by running the previous planner from `main` and the new planner on the same change, for a pull request, a push to `main`, and a release tag. Image names, build args, targets, and tags match, except the accepted extra `main` tag on default-branch runs.\n- The `latest` alias is published on every trusted default-branch run, including scheduled and manual (`workflow_dispatch`) runs on `main`, not only on pushes.\n- Publishing uses the `release` environment, which exists on this repository and allows the `main` branch and the `*/v*` and `v*` tags.\n\nBehaviour differences:\n\n- Pull requests build `amd64` only, on the standard hosted runner, with no registry login and no push. Previously pull requests built both architectures through the Docker build step, which pushes by digest.\n- Adds a daily scheduled run at 03:00 UTC. On `main` it is a trusted run and publishes the `latest` and `main` tags.\n- Adds `merge_group` triggers. The `develop` branch trigger from the template is omitted because the repository has no such branch.\n- `amd64` jobs run on `ubuntu-24.04` (previously `ubuntu-latest`). `arm64` jobs still run on `ubuntu-24.04-arm`.\n- Required status: the `result` job of the Build images run fails when any build or publish job fails.\n- The `VERSION` value on release tags is no longer exported to the runner environment. It is still passed as the `VERSION` build argument, so image contents are unchanged.\n\nSmoke tests: none. The previous caller did not run smoke tests and none are configured.\n\nOther workflows changed: none. The only workflow in `.github/workflows/` is the image caller replaced here.\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/ecosystem",
      "createdAt": "2026-11-19T13:00:30Z",
